.nh
.TH "PB-RECORDINGS-EXPORT" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-recordings-export - Write a recording as an asciicast v2 file


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb recordings export <recording-id> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Write one recording as an asciicast v2 file that standard players read. -o names the file;
without it the recording goes to standard output. The file is created readable by you only and
an existing file is never overwritten; a partial file is removed if the export fails. Like a
replay, the export is audited and needs your unlocked ENV vault. --archive reads the archived
copy in the team bucket instead of asking the machine.

.PP
This command does not support --json output; it rejects that mode before execution. Use --help --json for structured command help.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--archive\fP[=false]
	read the copy in the team bucket instead of asking the machine

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for export

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=""
	file to write; standard output when omitted


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb recordings export rec_abc123 -o session.cast
  pb recordings export rec_abc123 --archive > session.cast
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-recordings(1)\fP
